/-!
# The volume of an ellipsoid in shape-matrix form

For positive-definite `Q`, the Lebesgue measure of `{x | (x − q)ᵀ Q⁻¹ (x − q) ≤ 1}` is
`V_n √det Q`, `V_n = π^(n/2) / Γ(n/2 + 1)` the volume of the unit `n`-ball: [1, Sec. I (volume)]'s
`vol(B)/√det Q⁻¹` and [2, Eq. 2]'s `τ_n √det E`. The set is the ellipsoid generated by
`Q^(1/2)` (`mem_ofShape_iff`), a square generator, whose volume is `Ellipsoid.volume`
(`volume_eq_of_k_eq`) at the shape `Q` (`shape_ofShape`).

## References

* [1] A. Halder. "On the parameterized computation of minimum volume outer ellipsoid of
      Minkowski sum of ellipsoids". In Proc. of the 57th IEEE Conference on Decision and
      Control (CDC), pp. 4040-4045, 2018. arXiv:1803.08157.
* [2] M. Černý. "Goffin's algorithm for zonotopes". Kybernetika, 48(5):890-906, 2012.
-/

